# The image build needs only the module files and the packages the server is built from
# (Containerfile). Everything else, such as .git, bin/, a local .env or kubeconfig, stays out
# of the image build context. This doesn't limit an OpenShift binary build's upload:
# oc start-build --from-dir sends everything but .git to the cluster. Use --from-repo=.
# (committed files only) or --exclude to keep local files off the cluster.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!gen/
!internal/
**/.env
**/.env.*
